{title: Steadfast Love Forever}
{subtitle: Psalms 89:1–2}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]A maskil sung by Ethan the [Gm]Ezrahite
I [Eb]will sing [Bb]of the Lord's [Gm]steadfast love
[Eb]With my mouth [Bb]I make faithfulness known
[Cm7]To every gen[Fsus4]er[F]ation [Bb]that shall come
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Stead[F]fast love is [Gm]built [Gm7/D]to last [Eb]forever
In [Gm]the heav[F]ens you es[Bb]tablish [F]truth
I have said [Gm]so with [Gm7/D]my whole [Eb]heart
God's [F]faithful[Bb]ness [Bb]remains with you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I have made a covenant [Gm]with my chosen
[Eb]I have sworn to [Bb]David my ser[Gm]vant
I will [Eb]establish your [Bb]offspring forev[Cm7]er
And build your throne for all [Fsus4]genera[Bb]tions
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Steadfast love [F]is built to [Gm]last [Gm7/D]forev[Eb]er
In the heav[Gm]ens you es[F]tablish truth
[Bb]I have [F]said so with [Gm]my whole [Gm7/D]heart
God's [Eb]faithful[F]ness re[Bb]mains [Gm]with you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The prom[Eb]ise stands firm through [Bb]every age
[Gm]No shadow [Eb]falls upon [Bb]this vow
[Gm]Your mercy [Eb]endures beyond [Bb]time
[Cm7]A foundation strong and [Fsus4]sure now
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Steadfast [Bb]love is built to [F]last forev[Gm]er
In the [Eb]heavens you es[Gm]tablish [F]truth
I have [Bb]said so [F]with my whole [Gm]heart
God's faithful[Eb]ness re[F]mains with [Bb]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Sing of the grace that never [Gm]fades
[Eb]Declare the truth to all who [Bb]hear
[Eb]The covenant holds through every [Gm]storm
[Eb]Faithfulness [F]beyond all [Bb]fear
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
I will sing of the [F/A]Lord's love
For[Gm]ever and ever[Eb]more
[Bb]Steadfast love is built [F/A]to last
In the [Gm]heavens and on [Eb]the [Bb]shore
{end_of_verse}
